#            the report renderer. It accumulated the file into one string and
#            called `Buffer.byteLength(out)` per object to record that object's
#            cross-reference offset, so each of the 611 objects a 10,000-row
#            export produces re-encoded and re-scanned a rope ending at 2.8 MB.
#            2,000 rows 11.9 ms, 5,000 44.8, 10,000 147.3; counting each chunk
#            once as it is appended, 3.1 / 7.6 / 16.4 and linear.
#
