#            `latin1`, so every offset after the first character in
#            U+0080..U+00FF was too large by one per character. One `Société` in
#            a company name and the page's declared `/Length` overruns
#            `endstream` while `startxref` lands inside the `xref` keyword.
#            Post-escape every character is one Latin-1 byte, so `.length` is
#            both the right count and an O(1) one. **The existing `Ünïcode` test
#            could not see it**: it reads the output back as latin1, where the
#            string is fine — the defect was in the table of byte offsets beside
