#            content stream, resolves font descriptors and decodes every glyph
#            through them, and it is the dominant cost of an AI run whose
#            documents are PDFs, paid inline on the request. `_xlsx_text` was
#            worse in proportion — twenty sheets of two thousand rows is two
#            orders of magnitude past the budget, at a `_row_values` walk plus a
#            shared-strings lookup per cell. Measured on a twenty-sheet,
#            two-hundred-row workbook: 12.0 ms before, 0.7 ms after. Both stop
#            once the characters the caller keeps have been produced, and the
#            prefix is unchanged. The declared ceilings stay behind the budget
#            for what it cannot bound: a scan of images yields no characters per
#            page, an empty sheet none per row.
