#            the DLOM closed forms, the Longstaff bound, the Hamada levering,
#            the ASC 360/350 impairment tests, the LP catch-up and the
#            convertible lattice all reconcile against their published forms.
#
#            **A cliff off the cadence grid vested nothing on the day it
#            cleared.** `vestingStatus` floors the elapsed months to the vesting
#            cadence so a quarterly grant only vests on quarter boundaries, and
#            that flooring also swallowed the cliff: `Math.floor(6 / 12) * 12`
#            is 0, so a 6-month cliff on an annual cadence — or a 12-month cliff
#            on a 5-month one — reported `cliffCleared: true` and
#            `vestedShares: 0` on the same object, until the first cadence point
#            after it. The function's own docstring says the pro-rata amount
#            vests at once at the cliff. Nothing pairs the two figures at any
